data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

**Sync I/O via the Cosmos DB provider is fully removed.** In .NET 10, you had the sync-over-async opt-in (`CosmosOptionsExtension` flag). In EF Core 11, that opt-in no longer exists — all synchronous calls **always throw** at runtime, with no workaround.

Your broken methods: `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, and `SaveChanges()`.

### Fix: Convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

You'll also need to propagate `async`/`await` up through your callers (controllers, services, etc.). There is **no opt-in to restore** the old sync behavior — the Cosmos SDK is async-only and EF Core 11 enforces that completely.
